    <div class="cc-pl-row__img-wrap"><img src="/images/casper-cloaking-film-philadelphia-row1.webp" alt="Casper Cloaking Film technology on Philadelphia office glass partition hiding LED and LCD screen content" title="Casper Cloaking Film technology Philadelphia" width="768" height="960" loading="lazy" class="cc-pl-row__img" /><span class="cc-pl-row__pill">The Technology</span></div>
    <div class="cc-pl-row__content">
      <span class="cc-pl-row__num">01</span><span class="cc-pl-row__eyebrow">Proprietary Optical Filtration · LED & LCD Screens</span>
      <h3 class="cc-pl-row__heading">How a Film Applied to Glass Makes Every Screen in the Room Disappear</h3>
      <p class="cc-pl-row__body">Casper is built around selective optical filtration. Instead of blurring or frosting the glass, it targets the specific wavelengths emitted by LED and LCD screens. When someone looks through the treated glass from outside the room, the screen image is filtered out and appears black, while the rest of the room remains visible.</p>
      <p class="cc-pl-row__body">The film is applied to the interior surface of glass office partitions and conference room walls, making it a practical retrofit for existing Philadelphia offices. It does not hide printed documents, whiteboards, e-ink displays, OLED screens, furniture, or people; it is engineered specifically for compatible screen emissions and clear-glass interiors.</p>
      <div class="cc-pl-row__specs">
        <div class="cc-pl-row__spec"><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-val">LED & LCD</span><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-label">Screen Types</span></div>
        <div class="cc-pl-row__spec"><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-val">Interior</span><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-label">Surface</span></div>
        <div class="cc-pl-row__spec"><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-val">100%</span><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-label">Screen Blackout</span></div>
        <div class="cc-pl-row__spec"><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-val">~80%+</span><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-label">VLT</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-pl-row__pdfs">
        <span class="cc-pl-row__pdfs-label">Casper Technical Documents</span>
        <ul class="cc-pl-row__pdf-list">
          <li><a href="/resources/casper-cloaking-film-overview-philadelphia.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cc-pl-row__pdf-link"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>Casper Cloaking Film Overview</a></li>
          <li><a href="/resources/casper-cloaking-film-steelcase-brochure-philadelphia.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cc-pl-row__pdf-link"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>Steelcase Casper Brochure</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="cc-pl-row__warranty-note">5-year commercial warranty. Interior application on compatible glass. Source: Designtex / Steelcase.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cc-pl-row cc-pl-row--rev fade-in">
    <div class="cc-pl-row__img-wrap"><img src="/images/casper-cloaking-film-philadelphia-intro.webp" alt="Casper Clear film on Philadelphia glass conference room partition with invisible appearance until a screen turns on" title="Casper Clear screen privacy film Philadelphia" width="768" height="960" loading="lazy" class="cc-pl-row__img" /><span class="cc-pl-row__pill">Casper Clear</span></div>
    <div class="cc-pl-row__content">
      <span class="cc-pl-row__num">02</span><span class="cc-pl-row__eyebrow">Optically Invisible · No Visual Change to the Glass</span>
      <h3 class="cc-pl-row__heading">Casper Clear — Completely Invisible Until a Screen Turns On</h3>
      <p class="cc-pl-row__body">Casper Clear is the cleanest option for firms that want the glass to remain glass. The film is optically invisible in normal use, so hallway views into conference rooms, boardrooms, huddle spaces, and executive offices stay open. The privacy effect becomes obvious only when a compatible screen is active behind the treated glass.</p>
      <p class="cc-pl-row__body">That makes Casper Clear a strong fit for law firms, private equity offices, medical suites, and tech companies that invested in transparent interiors and do not want visible film graphics. It supports screen privacy while preserving daylight, interior architecture, and the open-plan feel that Philadelphia office designers are trying to protect.</p>
      <div class="cc-pl-row__specs">
        <div class="cc-pl-row__spec"><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-val">~80%+</span><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-label">VLT</span></div>
        <div class="cc-pl-row__spec"><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-val">Clear</span><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-label">Optics</span></div>
        <div class="cc-pl-row__spec"><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-val">Interior</span><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-label">Application</span></div>
        <div class="cc-pl-row__spec"><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-val">None</span><span class="cc-pl-row__spec-label">Color Shift</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-pl-row__pdfs">
        <span class="cc-pl-row__pdfs-label">Casper Technical Documents</span>
        <ul class="cc-pl-row__pdf-list">
          <li><a href="/resources/casper-cloaking-film-spec-sheet-philadelphia.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cc-pl-row__pdf-link"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>Casper Clear Spec Sheet</a></li>
          <li><a href="/resources/casper-cloaking-film-installation-instructions-philadelphia.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cc-pl-row__pdf-link"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>Installation Instructions</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="cc-pl-row__warranty-note">Casper Clear is optically clear — invisible on glass until a screen turns on. 5-year commercial warranty. Source: Designtex.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cc-pl-row fade-in">
    <div class="cc-pl-row__img-wrap"><img src="/images/casper-cloaking-film-philadelphia-row3.webp" alt="Patterned and custom printed Casper Cloaking Film on Philadelphia office glass with branded graphics" title="Patterned and custom Casper Cloaking Film Philadelphia" width="768" height="960" loading="lazy" class="cc-pl-row__img" /><span class="cc-pl-row__pill">Patterned & Custom</span></div>
    <div class="cc-pl-row__content">
      <span class="cc-pl-row__num">03</span><span class="cc-pl-row__eyebrow">Geometric Designs · Branded Options · Custom Printing</span>
      <h3 class="cc-pl-row__heading">Screen Privacy That Also Does Interior Design Work</h3>
      <p class="cc-pl-row__body">Casper Patterned combines the screen-cloaking function with decorative glass design. Geometric patterns and frosted design language can add visual rhythm to conference room walls, mark privacy zones, and soften long glass corridors while still protecting LED and LCD screen content from hallway views.</p>
      <p class="cc-pl-row__body">Custom printing brings brand logos, environmental graphics, wayfinding, and Philadelphia-specific interior themes into the Casper substrate. Creative firms, coworking spaces, university innovation labs, and client-facing offices can use Casper as both a privacy technology and a branded design surface.</p>
