<section class="cc-faq" id="faq"><div class="cc-faq__inner"><div class="cc-faq__header fade-in"><span class="cc-eyebrow">Questions</span><h2 class="cc-faq__title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><p>Honest answers about Casper Cloaking Film in Philadelphia from commercial privacy film specialists.</p><a href="/contact/" class="cc-faq__cta-btn">Talk to a Specialist</a></div><div class="cc-faq__list fade-in">
      <div class="cc-faq__item cc-faq__item--open">
        <div class="cc-faq__q"><span>What is Casper Cloaking Film and how does it work?</span><span class="cc-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="cc-faq__a"><p>Casper Cloaking Film is proprietary optical film technology made by Designtex, a Steelcase brand. Applied to the interior surface of glass office partitions, it selectively filters the wavelengths emitted by LED and LCD screens so screen content appears completely black from outside the glass while people, furniture, whiteboards, and daylight remain visible.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-faq__item">
        <div class="cc-faq__q"><span>Does it work on all screens?</span><span class="cc-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="cc-faq__a"><p>Casper works on LED and LCD displays. It does not cloak printed materials, whiteboards, e-ink displays, OLED screens, or non-emissive objects. During the site visit, Window Film Philadelphia confirms screen type, viewing angles, and partition layout before specifying the installation.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-faq__item">
        <div class="cc-faq__q"><span>Can people still see into the room?</span><span class="cc-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="cc-faq__a"><p>Yes. Casper Clear preserves the open glass-wall aesthetic because it targets screen light, not the room itself. People, furniture, daylight, and the architecture of the space remain visible from the hallway; only LED and LCD screen content is blacked out.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-faq__item">
        <div class="cc-faq__q"><span>Does it reduce natural light?</span><span class="cc-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="cc-faq__a"><p>Casper Clear maintains high visible light transmission, approximately 80% or more, so the glass remains bright and optically clear. Patterned and custom printed Casper options vary by design density, but they are still intended for interior glass partitions where daylight and openness matter.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-faq__item">
        <div class="cc-faq__q"><span>Is it available in patterns/decorative options?</span><span class="cc-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="cc-faq__a"><p>Yes. Casper is available as Casper Clear, patterned Casper designs, and custom printed graphics. Philadelphia firms can use geometric patterns, frosted design language, logos, or environmental graphics while still adding the screen-cloaking function to conference room glass.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-faq__item">
        <div class="cc-faq__q"><span>How is it different from frosted film?</span><span class="cc-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="cc-faq__a"><p>Frosted film blocks the full view through glass. Casper is screen-only privacy: it makes LED and LCD screens appear black from outside while preserving visibility into the room. That makes it a better fit for firms that want data privacy without closing off the space.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-faq__item">
        <div class="cc-faq__q"><span>What industries use it in Philadelphia?</span><span class="cc-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="cc-faq__a"><p>Casper is used by law firms, financial services offices, private equity teams, healthcare suites, technology companies, coworking spaces, university spinoffs, and boardrooms with glass partitions. It is especially useful in Center City, University City, the Navy Yard, and other Philadelphia offices where hallway traffic passes conference rooms.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cc-faq__item">
        <div class="cc-faq__q"><span>Who installs Casper in Philadelphia?</span><span class="cc-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="cc-faq__a"><p>Window Film Philadelphia installs Casper Cloaking Film for commercial interiors across Philadelphia. The team assesses the glass partition, screen technology, viewing angles, pattern goals, and warranty requirements before recommending Casper Clear, Casper Patterned, or a custom printed solution.</p></div>
      </div>
</div></div></section>

